is so important when hardware fails.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"17\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"18\">What should I do immediately if my SSD stops responding?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"19\">The most important step is to power down your system right away and unplug the SSD. If you keep it powered on-especially if it keeps disappearing from your computer-it might trigger the TRIM command, which could wipe your data forever. Call us for a check-up as soon as you can.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"20\">Can you recover data from an SSD that has been encrypted?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"21\">Yes, we can. Our recovery process works on the physical and firmware levels of the drive. Once we have a good forensic clone of the data, you can use your original encryption keys to unlock the files, as long as the data itself is okay.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"22\">Is my recovered data kept private?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23\">Absolutely. We follow very strict privacy and data protection rules. Your data is only accessed for the recovery job itself, and all recovered info is kept in a super secure, encrypted system.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"26\">How long does a typical SSD recovery take?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"27\">Most standard cases are finished within 2 to 3 days. If the recovery needs complex chip-level work or a huge amount of data transfer, it might take a bit longer, but we will always tell you what to expect after we check your drive.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"28\">What is the advantage of using a professional lab over DIY software?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"29\">Professional labs have the forensic tools needed to fix controller and firmware errors that simple software can&#8217;t reach. If you try to use generic software on a failing SSD, you might cause a &#8220;cascading failure&#8221; that makes the data gone forever-even for us!</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"30\">Start Your Professional SSD Recovery Today</h2>\