nts, or private records never leave our sight. We treat your information with the same level of care that you would, keeping everything totally confidential from the moment we get your drive until it’s safely back with you.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"11\">Moreover, we are deeply familiar with the unique needs of the Abu Dhabi business community and the wider UAE industrial sector. We understand that you need reliable, fast results that don&#8217;t cut corners on security. Whether you need a quick file rescue or a large-scale enterprise SAN restoration, we offer a very transparent policy on most projects. This ensures that you are only paying for real results. Our technicians aren’t just mechanics; they’re data forensic specialists who understand how important every single sector on your drives is. When you pick us, you’re choosing a partner who values your business as much as you do.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"12\">Real-World Success:</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"13\">A manufacturing facility in the Abu Dhabi Industrial City recently had a major crash on their primary server’s RAID 5 array. Because of a sudden power outage, the RAID controller didn&#8217;t write the final data bits correctly, which caused a logical &#8220;crash&#8221; that made their inventory database and logistics software impossible to open. Their internal IT team tried to force the array to come back online, but unfortunately, that just made the file system errors worse.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"13\">They called us for emergency help. Our engineers performed a clean-room component-level repair on the drives and then used our special software to manually reassemble the RAID striping pattern. Within 48 hours, we had successfully recovered 100% of their database. The facility was able to start working again quickly, avoiding a lot of lost money and contract trouble.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"14\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"15\">What should I do immediately after a server array warning?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"16\">Power down the system right away and unplug the power supply. Do not try to run a &#8220;rebuild&#8221; or &#8220;check disk&#8221; utility, as these can perform write operations that permanently destroy data on a corrupted array. Contact us for a professional assessment instead.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"17\">Can you recover data if my server controller board is burnt out?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"18\">Yes, we can. Our process involves cloning the individual drives and then using software to rebuild the controller&#8217;s logic. We don&#8217;t actually need your original controller board to rebuild the array, as long as the drives themselves are still physically okay.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"19\">How does a RAID 5 failure differ from a RAID 10 failure?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"20\">A RAID 5 failure often involves losing the math that keeps the data safe, making the array very sensitive to further drive issues. A RAID 10 failure can sometimes be a bit easier to recover, as long as the &#8220;mirror&#8221; sets are still good. We have the experience to handle both kinds.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"23\">How long does a typical server array reconstruction take?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"24\">Most standard cases are finished within 48 to 72 hours. If the recovery needs really complex work or transferring a huge amount of data, it might take a few extra days, but we’ll always give you a clear timeline after the first diagnosis.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"25\">Are my files secure during the recovery process?</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"26\">Absolutely. We follow very strict privacy and data protection rules. Your data is never touched for any reason other than the recovery, and all your recovered info is kept in a fully encrypted environment.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"27\">Start Your Professional Recovery Today</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28\">When a storage failure threatens your wor