data-path-to-node=\"21,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"21,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Monolithic Chip Recovery:</b> We use micro-soldering under high-power microscopes. This lets us tap into the &#8220;pin-out&#8221; traces of all-in-one USB drives. We extract raw data even without a visible circuit board to repair.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"21,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"21,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">USB Controller Emulation:</b> When a controller fails but the NAND is healthy, we use specialized hardware. Tools like the PC-3000 Flash emulate the original controller. This helps us rebuild the logical translator and access files.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"21,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"21,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Physical Connector Repair:</b> We provide precision soldering for snapped USB-A, USB-C, or Lightning connectors. This fixes drives that users accidentally kick or step on while plugged in.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"21,3,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"21,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Forensic File Carving:</b> For accidental deletion, we use deep-level carving tools. These search for file headers and signatures to reassemble fragmented documents that standard software misses.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"22\">Major Flash Architectures We Support</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Standard USB 2.0/3.0/3.1 Drives:</b> We offer full support for all major brands like SanDisk, Kingston, Samsung, and Transcend.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">USB-C &amp; OTG Mobile Drives:</b> More professionals now use dual-connector drives for MacBooks and phones. We have developed specialized workflows for these hybrid mobile storage devices.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Encrypted &amp; Secure Flash Drives:</b> We retrieve data from hardware-encrypted volumes like Kingston IronKe