data-path-to-node=\"17\">Comprehensive SSD Drive Recovery International City: Every Interface, Every Brand</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"18\">There are many different types of SSDs out there now. Our lab can handle every version found in the UAE market:</p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"19\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"19,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"19,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">NVMe and M.2 PCIe SSD Recovery:</b> These are in the new MacBooks and fast gaming PCs. They are very fast but very hard to fix. We specialize in repairing the boards and emulating the controllers for these.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"19,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"19,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Enterprise SSD and RAID Restoration:</b> For businesses in International City or DSO, we help with failed server arrays. If your server is down, our team works day and night to get your databases back.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"19,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"19,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">SATA and External Portable SSDs:</b> Whether it is a Samsung T7 or a basic internal drive, we fix everything from broken USB plugs to failed memory banks.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"19,3,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"19,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Chip-Off and Controller Bypass:</b> This is the most advanced tech we have. If the main chip is totally fried, we can &#8220;lift&#8221; the memory chips off and read them raw. Then we manually put the data back together for you.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"21\">Common SSD Failures We Resolve in our International City Data Recovery Shop</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"22\">The first thing we do is figure out exactly why the drive failed. In our <b data-path-to-node=\"22\" data-index-in-node=\"73\">International City data recovery shop</b>, we see these problems a lot:</p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"23\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Electronic Short-Circuits:</b> Usually caused by power spikes in the UAE or bad chargers. This can &#8220;kill&#8221; the power chip on the SSD.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Firmware Bugs:</b> This is a software failure inside the drive. The drive might show up as 0MB or have a weird name instead of showing your files.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Controller Failure:</b> The most common reason for &#8220;no media&#8221; errors. The memory chips are fine, but the &#8220;gatekeeper&#8221; chip is dead.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,3,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Accidental Deletion &amp; TRIM:</b> SSDs have a feature called TRIM that wipes deleted stuff fast to stay speedy. If you have a <b data-path-to-node=\"23,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"120\">formatted SSD data recovery International City</b> problem, turn it off now! If you wait, TRIM might erase everything forever.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,4,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,4,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Physical Damage:</b> Smashed laptops or dropped external drives often have cracked boards. We use microscopic soldering to fix them.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"23,5,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"23,5,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">End of Life:</b> Every SSD can only write data a certain amount of times. When it hits the limit, it might lock up or stop working.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"25\">Our Secure 4-Step SSD Data Recovery International City Process</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"26\">We want things to be simple so you don&#8217;t have to worry. Here is how we handle your <b data-path-to-node=\"26\" data-index-in-node=\"83\">SSD crash data recovery International City</b> case:</p>\n<ol start=\"1\" data-path-to-node=\"27\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"27,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"2