Why Servers Fail in Sharjah</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"4\">Server systems are much more complicated than a regular laptop. Because they use things like RAID, virtual machines, and super-fast SAS drives, even a tiny mistake can lock the whole system.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"4\">We get a lot of calls from IT managers when they see a <b data-path-to-node=\"4\" data-index-in-node=\"246\">server not booting after RAID failure Sharjah</b> businesses often deal with during power blips or when hardware gets a bit old. Unlike a simple hard drive fix, a server needs someone to rebuild the whole logical &#8220;map&#8221; of the data.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"5\">Also, the heat here in the UAE is a real enemy for servers. Even with good AC, the constant heat can wear out the electronic parts inside. If your team is stuck looking for a <b data-path-to-node=\"5\" data-index-in-node=\"175\">RAID controller &#8220;Foreign Configuration&#8221; error fix</b>, it usually means the &#8220;brain&#8221; of the server doesn&#8217;t recognize the disks anymore.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"5\">Please, don&#8217;t try to &#8220;force&#8221; the settings or &#8220;initialize&#8221; anything  that’s the quickest way to lose everything for good. At Recovery Data, we use special tools to talk to the drives safely and pull the data out without making the damage worse.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"6\">Common Server Problems We Solve Every Day</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"7\">Our lab is ready for almost any big storage problem, like:</p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"8\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"8,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"8,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">RAID Controller Death:</b> When the main card that controls all the disks just fries.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"8,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"8,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Mechanical Crashes:</b> When several disks in a group fail at the exact same time.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"8,2,0\"><b data-path-