ral Disasters</b>: We recover data from hardware damaged by fire, water, or the power surges that happen a lot in Al Barsha&#8217;s business zones.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,5,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,5,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Failed Rebuilds</b>: Saving data when an array fails while you&#8217;re trying to sync a new drive.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,6,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,6,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">NAS Specific Issues</b>: Fixing system or file problems in Synology, QNAP, or Buffalo devices.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,7,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,7,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">SAN Failures</b>: Handling connectivity loss that leaves your data totally isolated.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"11\">Why Corporations Trust Recovery Data for Enterprise Data Recovery Al Barsha 2</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12\">Trust is everything when it comes to data. When a business hands over its private financial records or client lists, they need more than just a promise; it needs a certified professional environment. Recovery Data is different because we invest in high-end tech and have a very clear, honest way of doing business.</p>\n<h6 data-path-to-node=\"13\">ISO Class 5 Cleanroom for Physical Server Drive Repair</h6>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"14\">You can&#8217;t just open a server drive in a normal office. Even one tiny piece of dust can hit the disk and destroy your data forever. We do all our hardware &#8220;surgery&#8221; inside a local ISO Class 5 Cleanroom. This keeps your sensitive gear away from dirt and dust, which is something a regular repair shop just can&#8217;t offer.</p>\n<h6 data-path-to-node=\"15\">Strict Data Privacy Protocols and Legally Binding NDAs</h6>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"16\">We treat your data as carefully as a bank does. Our lab follows very strict privacy rules, and we give all our business clients a legal Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA). Your data is handled on sys