m. At Recovery Data, we have seen every possible failure mode. We have developed the protocols to reverse them.</p>\n<h3 data-path-to-node=\"8\">Every SD Card Issue We Resolve:</h3>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Physical Damage:</b> We handle snapped casings or cracked Micro SD cards using specialized monolithic recovery techniques.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Salt Water Corrosion:</b> This often occurs for cards used in drones or GoPros near the Palm’s beaches.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Logical Corruption:</b> Sudden power loss during a write cycle often creates a RAW file system.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,3,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Accidental Formatting:</b> We frequently assist clients who re-initialize a card in-camera before backing up their shoot.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,4,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,4,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">&#8220;Card Not Recognized&#8221;:</b> This typically happens when the internal controller chip fails.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,5,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,5,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">NAND Flash Degradation:</b> Often called &#8220;bit rot,&#8221; this results from long-term storage or excessive read/write cycles.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,6,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,6,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Encryption Lock:</b> We recover data from cards used in high-security Android devices or professional encrypted cameras.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"9,7,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"9,7,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Virus/Malware:</b> Our lab strips away malicious software that hides folders or turns files into shortcuts.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"11\">Why Elite Palm Jumeirah Residents Trust Recovery Data</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"12\">Residents of the Palm demand service that reflects exce