damaged capacitors and &#8220;bridged&#8221; the power directly to the storage chips. This allowed our forensic tools to communicate with the CPU. <b data-path-to-node=\"34\" data-index-in-node=\"305\">In the end</b>, we successfully recovered 100% of the client’s project files, totaling over 800GB of data, within 48 hours. <b data-path-to-node=\"34\" data-index-in-node=\"425\">Clearly</b>, this is the level of expertise that makes us the go-to provider for <b data-path-to-node=\"34\" data-index-in-node=\"502\">professional Mac data recovery Karama</b>.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"36\">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"37\"><b data-path-to-node=\"37\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Can you recover data from a dead M1/M2/M3 MacBook?</b> Yes, we can. While these chips are highly integrated, we use specialized logic board repair techniques to bypass failed components. <b data-path-to-node=\"37\" data-index-in-node=\"183\">This allows</b> us to access the storage area even if the Mac will not boot.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"38\"><b data-path-to-node=\"38\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">How much does professional Mac data recovery cost in Karama?</b> The cost depends on the type of failure rather than the amount of data. <b data-path-to-node=\"38\" data-index-in-node=\"133\">For example</b>, physical repairs requiring donor parts are more complex than simple software fixes. We provide a fixed-price quote after our free diagnosis.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"39\"><b data-path-to-node=\"39\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">How long does the Apple Mac data recovery process take?</b> Standard recovery typically takes 3 to 5 business days. <b data-path-to-node=\"39\" data-index-in-node=\"112\">However</b>, for urgent cases, our <b data-path-to-node=\"39\" data-index-in-node=\"143\">emergency Mac data recovery Karama</b> team can often deliver results within 24 to 48 hours.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"40\"><b data-path-to-node=\"40\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Is it