very fast imaging tools and a team that works overnight, we can often give you a list of files just a few hours after you bring the drives to our lab.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"26\">Common Problems We Fix Every Day</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"27\">Our technical team is trained to find and fix all kinds of storage failures. We handle these things daily for our clients in Al Barsha Heights:</p>\n<ul data-path-to-node=\"28\">\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,0,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">RAID Controller Failure:</b> When the main hardware dies and the system forgets how the drives work together.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,1,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,1,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Multiple Drive Failure:</b> In RAID 5 or 6, when too many drives die at the same time.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,2,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,2,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Accidental Formatting:</b> When someone accidentally wipes the array or deletes a partition.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,3,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,3,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Firmware Issues:</b> When the NAS won&#8217;t start because of a bad update.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,4,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,4,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Mechanical Drive Problems:</b> Clicking or grinding noises coming from the server.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,5,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,5,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Power Surge Damage:</b> Fried parts caused by unstable electricity.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,6,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,6,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Ransomware:</b> Data locked by a virus; we help you get back in.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"28,7,0\"><b data-path-to-node=\"28,7,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">File System Errors:</b> Problems with things like ZFS or Btrfs that stop the data from showing up.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\