ompany from huge fines and a lot of trouble.</p>\n<h2 data-path-to-node=\"34\">Frequently Asked Questions About NAS Data Recovery</h2>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"35\"><b data-path-to-node=\"35\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">How much does NAS recovery cost in Sharjah?</b> The price for <b data-path-to-node=\"35\" data-index-in-node=\"58\">NAS hard drive recovery services SAIF Zone</b> depends on how many drives you have and what kind of damage there is. We give you a free check-up and a fixed price quote so there are no hidden costs.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"36\"><b data-path-to-node=\"36\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Can you recover data if two drives failed in RAID 5?</b> Yes, we can. Even though RAID 5 is only &#8220;supposed&#8221; to handle one failure, we can often fix the broken disks in our Cleanroom just long enough to get the data off. This is how we finish a <b data-path-to-node=\"36\" data-index-in-node=\"240\">RAID NAS recovery SAIF Zone</b> even when the math says it’s impossible.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"37\"><b data-path-to-node=\"37\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">How long does it take?</b> Most jobs take about 3 to 5 business days. If it&#8217;s a huge emergency, we have a faster service that can get things done in 24 to 48 hours, depending on how bad the drives are hurt.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"38\"><b data-path-to-node=\"38\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Is it okay to try and &#8220;rebuild&#8221; the NAS myself?</b> If you don&#8217;t have a backup, please don&#8217;t try it! The rebuilding process is very hard on the drives. If another drive has even one tiny weak spot, the whole thing will crash and you might lose your data forever.</p>\n<p data-path-to-node=\"39\"><b data-path-to-node=\"39\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Do you pick up the drives in SAIF Zone?</b> Yes! We offer free and safe pickup for any business or person in the <b data-path-to-node=\"39\" data-index-in-node=\"109\">Sharjah Airport International Free Zone</b> and the areas nearby.</p>\n<